P18-V01 RequestResponseFuture nullable latch slice (2026-10-16 06:16 UTC)

- Compared the pinned Java 5.5.1 fixture behavior with the Rust future and reply path. Java accepts a null CountDownLatch; `putResponseMessage` stores the response before throwing `NullPointerException`, and `waitResponseMessage` also throws. Inbound reply handling leaves the table entry present when completion fails and acknowledges `SYSTEM_ERROR`.
- Implemented Rust `Option` latch accessors, typed `RequestFutureError` results, and an async no-deadline latch wait. Reply completion now propagates the missing-latch error to inbound handling while retaining response state and correlation-table ownership. Added Rust future, inbound, and facade regressions.
- Added Java fixture coverage and regenerated `fixtures/producer/request-reply.json`. The first standalone `exec:java` call used stale compiled classes; the first fixture drift check and facade fixture assertion consequently failed. Recompiled with `mvn -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml compile exec:java ...`, regenerated the fixture, and reran the checks successfully. Maven `verify` passed after regeneration.
- Passed: `cargo test --locked -p rocketmq-classic-core --lib` (167 tests); `cargo test --locked -p rocketmq-classic-producer --test request_reply` (3 tests); `cargo test --locked -p rocketmq-classic --test request_reply_public_api` (5 tests); strict all-target/all-feature Clippy for Core, Producer, and facade; `cargo fmt --all -- --check`; `git diff --check`; pinned Java 5.5.1 Maven `verify` (37 scenarios, fixture drift and cross-decode gates).
- Code commit: `310b6cd6`; Java/fixture commit: `3be59a09`. Updated Phase 15 and Phase 6 compatibility records and the release checklist. Plans and the external Java reference checkout were not modified.
- Still open: broad P18-V01 bidirectional source/API/input/error/control-flow and reverse-export audit; a full P18-V02 rerun on this new code revision; current-revision Ubuntu/P18-V04 evidence; Phase 19 Docker/Broker runner and scenario execution; owner-validation instructions; release version/registry preflight. Production/deployment verification remains manual.
